{
  "message": "Thanks — I can help. To start verification, please give either the full name on the account (case‑sensitive), the email address on file, or your user ID. After you provide one of those, I’ll ask you to confirm any 2 of these on‑file items: date of birth, email, phone number, or address. Which identifier would you like to provide now?"
}

{
  "message": "Done — I raised your Green card ATM limit to $900 for the next 24 hours. Try your withdrawal again. A couple of reminders:

- This increase applies on our side, but some non‑Rho ATMs enforce their own per‑transaction limits. If the ATM still declines, try a different machine or make smaller withdrawals.
- The increase expires in 24 hours and will revert to $600.

Would you like me to (A) attempt anything on your Blue card as well (note: Blue had an overdraft fee on 11/01, so a temporary increase isn’t allowed), (B) look up the teen account limits and parental controls, (C) locate the nearest Rho-Bank ATM to you, or (D) transfer you to a human agent?"
}

{
  "message": "Thanks — here’s what happened and your options right now.",
  "blue_card_summary": {
    "what_failed": "Your Blue card attempt for $300 likely exceeded the card’s remaining daily ATM allowance.",
    "evidence": "Today your Blue account already had ~$400 in ATM withdrawals (seen in posted activity). Blue daily ATM limit = $500, so you had about $100 remaining — a $300 attempt would push past the daily limit and be declined.",
    "temporary_increase": "I can’t request a temporary increase for the Blue card because there’s an overdraft fee posted on 11/01/2025 (policy requires no overdraft fees in the last 30 days)."
  },
  "options_for_blue": [
    "Withdraw up to $100 now from the Blue card (that’s the remaining daily allowance).",
    "Use your Green card (now temporarily increased to $900) to withdraw the full amount you need.",
    "Try a different ATM or a Rho‑Bank ATM (some third‑party ATMs enforce their own per‑transaction limits)."
  ],
  "sofia_teen_card": {
    "typical_limits": "Light Green (teen) ATM daily limit = $150.",
    "possible_reasons_for_decline": [
      "Her daily ATM limit may already be used up for the day.",
      "Parental controls on the teen account could block ATM use or certain terminal types (these controls must be changed by the primary guardian in the app or branch).",
      "The ATM terminal itself could be flagged (try another machine).",
      "Physical card damage or a card status (FROZEN/INACTIVE) — unlikely if you didn’t see a freeze, but possible."
    ],
    "next_step_offer": "If you want, I can check Sofia’s Light Green account status (today’s ATM usage and card status) and confirm why the withdrawal declined. To do that I’ll need Sofia’s full name exactly as on her account and your confirmation that you’re the authorized guardian and want me to check."
  },
  "recommendation": "Fastest way to get cash to the tow truck: use your Green card at a nearby ATM (you can withdraw up to $900 now) or withdraw $100 from Blue and then $200 from Green. If you want, I can: (A) locate the nearest Rho‑Bank ATM to you, (B) check Sofia’s teen card now (I’ll need her full name and your authorization), or (C) connect you to a human agent. Which should I do?"
}
